  words:
  - bee
  - bees
  info: "Bees are winged insects in the order Hymenoptera. The most well-known bee
    species are bumble bees and honey bees. Bees are known for being social insects
    that live in hierarchical colonies, but over 90% of bee species are solitary.
    \n\nHoney bees are known to build hives out of hexagonal cells that can store
    honey and larvae. Honey bees are also important for the environment as they pollinate
    35% of the world's crop and 75% of flowering plants.\n\nSources: \nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bee\nhttps://www.unep.org/news-and-stories/story/why-bees-are-essential-people-and-planet"
  image: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 34e766f3297416a44b7503079d74b01d, type: 3}
